I'm refering the spoiler art1-343 found here:

http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/art1-343.txt

relevant quotes:

"You will only get artifacts that are of your alignment or none, and
some classes get certain artifacts as their first gift (if available).
Your first gift will always be co-aligned. Orcs will never receive
elven weapons, or vice versa. The chance that you will be given a gift
depends on the number of artifacts already created in the game and how
many of them were gifts; the chance is 1/(10+(2*artifacts*gifts))."

"if you are of the same class as the artifact, you can only obtain it
by completing your Quest. Otherwise it can only be obtained by bones
levels or wishing. If you are neither the same class nor the same
alignment, you cannot pick it up, wield it, or wear it."

"The chance of getting an artifact from each wish depends on the number
of artifacts already created in the game:
        ARTIFACTS   0     1     2     3    4    5    6      n
        CHANCE     100%  100%  2/3   2/4  2/5  2/6  2/7  2/(n+1)"

So, I'd say your best bet is still to altar camp if you already have
"quite a few" artifacts. It will take a while, but it will eventually
happen. You'll get chaotic and neutral artifacts, but never any quest
or lawful artifacts.



